
# Gloss — an interlinear gloss: each source word stacked over its grammatical gloss, aligned in reading order. A
# reusable widget a package document embeds. Headless (data-slot hooks). Props:
#   words -> list of { form, gloss }; `form` is the source-language word, `gloss` its interlinear label
#            (e.g. "walk-PST"). Lay the words in a row and stack form over gloss via CSS on [data-slot=gloss].

load @term/site/code/zone/render
  find element
  find text
load @term/site/code/dom/dom
  find view
  find append

zone gloss
  take host, like view
  take words
  zone div
    bind data-slot, text <gloss>
    walk list, read words
      hook next
        take site, name word
        zone div
          bind data-slot, text <gloss-word>
          zone div
            bind data-slot, text <gloss-form>
            read
              read word/form
          zone div
            bind data-slot, text <gloss-tag>
            read
              read word/gloss
